 # Working notes: 75d4884529f6
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current peer audit: unresolved demonstration coverage
+
+The unchanged generator can introduce a color-specific glyph in a query without
+showing that color in any demonstration. One bounded protected-Racket witness
+uses seed 4, default difficulty, sample indices 0–2 as demonstrations and 3 as
+query. No demonstration has color-6 markers. The fixed rival “color 6 makes an
+ordinary straight connection” matches all three reference demonstration outputs
+and differs on 13 query cells (first: row 4, column 2, reference 6, rival 0).
+Color-6 glyph geometry is therefore not identified by these visible pairs.
+
+Evidence: `workspace/peer_learnability_probe.py` and
+`workspace/peer_learnability_evidence.json`. Run from packet root:
+`WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run python3 generators/75d4884529f6/workspace/peer_learnability_probe.py`.
+The probe passed its witness assertions with eight protected Racket evaluations.
+It binds generator SHA-256
+`382e664c9d0d784b70ed72f2e5b25873e053745cc71fe2eb8bf33e491665a7e7`
+and the selected canonical program SHA-256
+`ac35f5632c11551fd859318df9d34de5f5817d83b6b54ff22155e9cbc10efa3f`.
+The probe resolves `Catalog.rule_task_id`, requires identical selected
+`program_solution` values in `shared/data/canonical/puzzles.jsonl`, and executes
+those exact bytes. This selected-canonical replay replaces the initial archival
+base-rule probe; it reproduces the same three demo matches and 13 query differences.
+Production source remains unchanged.
+Decision: retain as an unresolved teaching issue; demonstrate every query glyph
+before querying it, or restrict query colors to adequately demonstrated glyphs.
+Scope is one source-generated episode witness, not a prevalence estimate or a
+full battery. No task-local tests or review index were present at audit start.
