 ## 2026-10-03 — optional rotated-query observation
 
 A relocated shared-tool smoke produced two original three-demo/one-query lessons with zero ambiguity, but one of eight all-query rotations removed the sole counterexample to bbox completion, color agreement and repeated-application rivals. This is a finite observation, not a failure of the two production lessons. Exact source, seeds and query indices are in `evidence/maintainer-query-rotation-20261003.json`. Do not assume all query positions are interchangeable; recheck if changing lesson assembly. Generator source and authority are unchanged.
+
+Current bounded peer audit: `workspace/peer_rotation_probe.py` replayed this
+mechanism on four direct draws at seed `2546197209`, easy indices `1,2,3,4`.
+Protected bundled Racket supplied all four labels and agreed with the mirror.
+Demos `1,2,3` with query `4` left no declared rival alive; moving index `3`
+into the query left bbox completion, ignored color agreement, and repeated
+completion consistent with all three demos but wrong on the query. Evidence:
+`workspace/peer_rotation_evidence.json`, bound to source SHA-256
+`788832612d5ab93e59f99522fd2b89e72e8d1d2ca7776779f272c13f22d08cf5`.
+This confirms the existing limitation, with no new production issue found and
+no production-source changes. It is a mechanism replay, not a byte-identical
+reconstruction of the earlier materialized lesson or an exhaustive rival audit.
+Command from the packet root:
+`WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run python3 generators/78f3cf31c4bf/workspace/peer_rotation_probe.py`.
+
 ## Current reviewer considerations
 
 Source SHA-256: `788832612d5ab93e59f99522fd2b89e72e8d1d2ca7776779f272c13f22d08cf5`.
